# Email Configuration
# Replace with your actual email address
VITE_MY_EMAIL=your-email@example.com

# EmailJS Configuration
# Get these from your EmailJS dashboard (https://dashboard.emailjs.com/)
# 1. Create an account at EmailJS.com
# 2. Create a new service (Gmail, Outlook, etc.)
# 3. Create an email template
# 4. Get your public key from Account settings

# Service ID from EmailJS
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_service_id

# Template ID from EmailJS
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=your_template_id

# Public Key from EmailJS
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key

## Setup Instructions:
## 1. Copy this file to .env
## 2. Replace all placeholder values with your actual credentials
## 3. Make sure to configure your EmailJS template to send emails to the recipient email you want
## 4. Test the form locally before deploying